pkgsrc still carries older Emacsen, and some of the elisp it packages
was written for a later one.  This package installs, for the Emacs it
is built for, a file that defines only what is missing there.

For Emacs 20 that is e20-compat.el: hash tables, replace-regexp-in-string,
propertize, subr-x's string functions, setq-local, with-eval-after-load,
prog-mode, syntax-ppss, syntax-propertize, and a translator that rewrites
regexps using shy groups, intervals and [:alpha:] classes into what
Emacs 20's engine accepts, remapping the match data afterwards.

Emacs 21 and later have all of it, so nothing is installed for them.
